# Architecture — fieldops-app

This repository is the Expo FieldOps consuming app. Requirements define *what* ships.
These rules define *how* the codebase stays stable when dependencies or APIs change.

Record irreversible trade-offs in root `DECISIONS.md` per `030-decisions.mdc`.

## Product boundaries

- Expo SDK 57. Consumes `@pranadwaghmare2/fieldops-ui` as an npm package — not a relative import, not a monorepo.
- Three screens eventually: work-order list, detail, create/edit. Foundation may ship empty feature folders.
- Required libs (via integrations only): TanStack Query, Axios, React Hook Form, Zod, NativeWind.
- No auth, offline sync, settings, EAS, dark mode, or store publishing unless requirements change.

## Folder structure

```
app/                            # Expo Router shells only — no business logic
src/
  core/
    theme/                      # FieldOps tokens ONLY (match UI library preset)
    config/                     # JSON timeouts/limits + env loader
    constants/                  # copy + static config values (not enums/types)
    utils/                      # app-wide pure helpers (date, isApiError, toApiError, …)
    types/                      # shared enums, models, envelopes — no I/O
    integrations/
      http/                     # Axios client + thin httpGet/Post/… verbs only
      query/                    # QueryClient provider + wrappers + key factory
      form/                     # RHF + Zod adapters
      styling/                  # NativeWind host bridge
      ui/                       # re-export fieldops-ui components
      image/                    # expo-image adapter (AppImage)
  features/
    work-orders/
      list|detail|form/
        types/                  # feature-local types only
        services/               # resource paths + http* calls (no error/success map)
        hooks/                  # ViewModels
        components/
        screens/                # dumb UI
        constants/              # feature-local only
        utils/                  # feature-local only
mock-api/                       # do not modify server.js
```

### Dependency direction (enforced on every change)

```
core/theme|config|constants|utils|types
                ↓
        core/integrations/*
                ↓
       features/*/services
                ↓
          features/*/hooks
                ↓
     features/*/components|screens
                ↓
              app/
```

- Inner layers never import outer layers.
- `app/` imports screens (or thin placeholders) and providers from integrations — never Axios/Query/RHF/Zod package paths.
- Features never import third-party packages except `react` / `react-native` / `expo-router` navigation primitives as needed for UI. All other vendors enter only through `core/integrations/`.
- Changing Axios, Query, RHF, Zod, NativeWind, or `expo-image` edits `core/integrations/` only.
- Integrations = vendor adapters only (see `070-integrations.mdc`). Feature resource URLs live in `features/*/services`. Hooks call services; services call port APIs and pass through results. Pure error normalization (`toApiError`) lives in `core/utils`; vendor-shaped failure extraction stays inside the matching port.

---

### Layer: `core/theme`

**Responsibility:** Single source of FieldOps design values in the app for layout math and non-component styling.

**Contains:** colours, status→tone maps, spacing, typography, radius — same values as the brief / `@pranadwaghmare2/fieldops-ui` preset.

**Must not:** invent a second palette; dark theme; custom fonts; shadows; duplicate hex in features.

**Token contract:** `bg` `#FFFFFF`, `surface` `#F6F7F9`, `border` `#E3E6EA`, `fg` `#111827`, `fg-muted` `#6B7280`, `primary` `#1D4ED8`, `primary-fg` `#FFFFFF`, `danger` `#DC2626`, `warning` `#D97706`, `success` `#15803D`. Status: `open`→`fg-muted`, `in_progress`→`primary`, `blocked`→`warning`, `done`→`success`. Priority text-only except `urgent`→`danger`. Spacing 1=4…8=32. Radius 10. Hairline borders.

**SOLID:** S — tokens only. O — add tokens, do not fork per screen. D — everything reads tokens, nothing invents them.

---

### Layer: `core/config` | `constants` | `utils` | `types`

- **config** — timeouts, debounce ms, page size (JSON + typed loaders); `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` via env helper.
- **constants** — user-facing copy (`messages`) and other static non-type values. **Not** enums, interfaces, or domain models.
- **utils** — app-wide pure helpers (dates, `isApiError`, `toApiError` with `HttpStatus` switch, …). Feature-only helpers stay under that feature.
- **types** — shared enums (`Status`, `Priority`, `HttpStatus`, `ApiErrorKind`), models (`WorkOrder`, `User`), envelopes (`ApiSuccess`, `ApiError`, `CursorPage`, `TransportFailure`), and later mappers. No React, no I/O. Import as `@/core/types`.

---

### Layer: `core/integrations`

**Responsibility:** Isolate every third-party dependency behind a narrow adapter/provider port. One vendor family per folder. Swap the library by editing that port only.

**Ports:** `http`, `query`, `form`, `styling`, `ui`, `image` — details and ban table in `070-integrations.mdc` (do not duplicate the full table here).

**Must not:** implement product screens; own feature resource URLs or feature params types; own shared domain enums/models (those are `core/types`); put pure app error policy in a vendor file when it can live in `core/utils`.

**SOLID:** S — one adapter family per concern. O — new vendor behaviour as new/extended port. D — features depend on ports; integrations implement with vendors.

**Platform exception:** `react`, `react-native`, and Expo Router file routes may be used in `app/` and screens. Everything else goes through integrations.

---

### Layer: `features/*`

**Responsibility:** Feature slices with hook ViewModels and dumb screens/components.

**Per-area folders:** `types/`, `services/`, `hooks/`, `components/`, `screens/`, optional local `constants/`, `utils/`.

- Feature `types/` holds ViewModel return unions, filter unions, list params, and exported component prop types. Do not leave those in hook files as the only home.
- Feature `services/` own resource paths and call http verbs; return typed success data; do not catch/map errors or reshape envelopes.
- Shared models belong in `core/types`, not under a feature `types/` folder.

**Must not:** import Axios, `@tanstack/*`, `react-hook-form`, `zod`, `nativewind`, `@pranadwaghmare2/fieldops-ui`, `expo-image` by package path.

**SOLID:** S — screen = render; hook = orchestration; service = resource call. I — narrow ViewModel return shapes. D — hooks depend on services + query port; services depend on http verbs.

---

### Layer: `app/`

**Responsibility:** Expo Router entry, layouts, provider wiring, route → screen mapping.

**Must not:** contain business rules, API calls, form schemas, or Query key construction.

## Anti-patterns (reject in review)

- Feature file importing a vendor package that has an integrations port.
- Second colour theme or dark mode system.
- Collapsing this repo with `fieldops-ui` into a monorepo as the distribution model.
- Putting adapter code inside `features/*/`.
- Putting enums / shared interfaces in `core/constants` (they belong in `core/types`; constants are copy/config values).
- Putting feature resource URLs or fat API modules inside `core/integrations/*`.
- Feature UI state types living only inside hooks; shared models living under a feature `types/` folder.
- Hard-coding resource models (e.g. `WorkOrder`) on shared `ApiError`; owning `ApiError` types inside an integration port.
- Colocating `*.test.ts(x)` under `src/` (tests belong in top-level `tests/` — see `020-testing.mdc`).
- Logic-heavy `app/*.tsx` route files.
- Documenting architecture by name-dropping “clean” / “SOLID” without following the folder contracts above.
